=== HOW TO PICK A ROLL ===
- For an `attack_roll`: emit `attack_option_id` (verbatim — copy the
  exact id from LEGAL ATTACK OPTIONS, never invent one like
  "spell:shield" or "spell:mage_armor") and `target` (the participant
  name). Do NOT set `dc`. Do NOT set `damage` — both are resolved
  from the option + the target's sheet. If the spell the player named
  is NOT in LEGAL ATTACK OPTIONS, it is not an attack — see the
  buff / utility branch below.
- For a `saving_throw`: emit `save` (fort/ref/will) and `dc_formula`
  ({ kind: "spell_dc", spell_name, caster: "player" } or
  { kind: "ability_dc", pattern: "half_hd_plus_ability", origin_target,
  ability }). Do NOT set `dc`.
- For a `skill_check`: emit `skill` and `dc` from the matching rule
  above (or a sensible PF1e default if no rule fits). Defensive
  casting while threatened is a Concentration check (DC 15 + spell
  level). When the check is directed at a single creature in CAST
  ROSTER (Diplomacy on a guard, Stealth past a foe, Bluff to feint),
  also emit `target_creature_sheet_id` (an integer copied verbatim
  from the CAST ROSTER `id`). For opposed checks (Stealth, Bluff,
  Diplomacy, Disguise, Sleight of Hand, Intimidate) prefer to OMIT
  `dc` — the engine resolves the DC from the target's defending stat.
  Omit `target_creature_sheet_id` entirely (do NOT emit `null`) when
  the check has no creature target — Concentration, Climb, Acrobatics
  to stand from prone, etc. The id MUST come from CAST ROSTER above;
  never invent one.

=== BUFF / UTILITY SPELLS — NO ROLL ===
Self-buffs and personal utility spells (shield, mage armor, bless,
haste, longstrider, expeditious retreat, true strike, prot. from evil,
mirror image, blur, etc.) do NOT roll an attack and do NOT call for a
save. They just APPLY. For these:
  - Set `needs_roll: false`.
  - `no_roll_reason`: name the spell ("Shield is a self-buff, no roll").
  - Add a `consequences` entry that names the spell + duration in
    rounds (e.g. `{ "description": "Shield active for 1 minute (10 rounds): +4 shield bonus to AC, immune to magic missile." }`)
    so the context update applies it.
The exception is defensive casting while a foe threatens you — then
ALSO request a Concentration `skill_check` at DC 15 + spell level.

If nothing in the intent calls for a roll (the player only declares
position, draws a weapon, talks, etc.), set `needs_roll: false` with
a one-sentence `no_roll_reason`.

=== ACTION COST ===
Set `action_cost`: "standard" (default), "move", "swift", "free", or
"full_round". Most creative attacks are standard.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON in this exact FLAT shape (no wrapper keys):
{
  "needs_roll": true,
  "no_roll_reason": null,
  "roll": {
    "type": "attack_roll",
    "attack_option_id": "spell:42",
    "target": "Goblin",
    "description": "Cast scorching ray at the goblin.",
    "rule_slug": null
  },
  "target_creature_sheet_id": 273,
  "action_cost": "standard",
  "mechanical_summary": "One-sentence factual summary.",
  "reasoning": "One short sentence explaining the call."
}

`target_creature_sheet_id` belongs at the top level (NOT inside
`roll`). Omit it entirely for attack_roll/saving_throw/buff branches
and for skill_checks with no creature target. The example above shows
it filled in for clarity — most attack-roll responses will not include
it.
